# L §8 What a result reads and Refusals outrank holes (tally 2.1.7 R1, R2, issue #141; T's SR-1): pull[k1] and
# pull[k2] fall on one day with no ties by and each reads the balance of jar the other changes: RUN-TIE refuses each
# (L §5.14.2), so bal(jar) is refused (b). Their legs never give konto, so konto's ledger reads neither: a refused
# movement reaches exactly where a hole movement would, and the ledger is answered (led). 2.1.7's first refcore
# refused residuals konto by the tie.
=== sr1.tally
model sr1
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
source bank "bank"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [k1, k2]
input bank_rows: observed
input dday: date
input fee: money PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place jar: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place unexplained: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pull[k in ks]: transfers
  on dday
  reads jar
  leg cash from jar to world amount bal(jar) - fee

ask led: residuals konto 2026-02
ask b: bal(jar, 2026-03-01)

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  dday = 2026-02-10 "c"
  fee = 100.00 PLN "c"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
  opening[jar] = 800.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"

version statement_02
  cite bank
  governs 2026-02
  known 2026-03-02
  covers konto
  pad konto from unexplained
  bank_rows[r1] = (on: 2026-02-20, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 400.00 PLN) "line 1"
=== expect
b: refused: RUN-TIE pull has a tie at pull[k1], pull[k2] that changes the result, and no ties by
  unfulfilled: pull[k1]
  cut 2026-10-20
led: residuals konto 2026-02
  2026-02 unexplained: model 0.00 PLN, observed -400.00 PLN, difference -400.00 PLN
    unexplained bank_rows[r1] on 2026-02-20: observed -400.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
